Usage: install [OPTION]... [-T] SOURCE DEST
  install [OPTION]... SOURCE... DIRECTORY
  install [OPTION]... -t DIRECTORY SOURCE...

Copy files and set attributes.

Note: This Windows implementation supports copying, compare-and-skip,
timestamp preservation, and selected destination handling. Ownership,
group, strip, and SELinux context handling remain limited on Windows.

OPTIONS:
  -b, --backup                make a backup of each existing destination file
  -c                          (ignored)
  -C, --compare               compare source and destination and skip copy if
                              identical
  -d, --directory             treat all arguments as directory names
  -D                          create all leading components of DEST except the
                              last
  -g, --group ARG             set group ownership
  -m, --mode ARG              set permission mode
  -o, --owner ARG             set ownership
  -p, --preserve-timestamps   apply access/modification times of SOURCE files
  -s, --strip                 strip symbol tables
      --debug                 print debugging information
      --strip-program ARG     program used to strip binaries
  -S, --suffix ARG            override the usual backup suffix
  -t, --target-directory ARG  specify the destination directory
  -T, --no-target-directory   do not treat the last operand specially when it is
                              a directory
  -v, --verbose               print the name of each directory as it is created
      --preserve-context      preserve SELinux security context
  -Z                          set SELinux security context of destination files
                              to default
      --context[=ARG]         set SELinux security context of destination files
      --help                  display this help and exit
  -V, --version               output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
